From bbf15707c8999114d66bf73b2645ee04a47c7c27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Pavlovic <sam@sampavlovic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:36:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/36] grate: fragment uniforms, SLT/SGE/CMP, wider
 temporaries, and a test suite

Continues towards running a compositor. weston's gl-renderer now starts,
compiles its shaders and composites.

 - fragment uniforms: TGSI constants map to register file slots 32..63 and
   are uploaded as fp20 through REG_TGR3D_ALU_GLOBALS. The advertised
   constant buffer was 32 bytes, two vec4s, which weston's shaders could not
   link against; it now reflects the 32 scalars the hardware has.
 - SLT and SGE via the ALU condition code, which forces the result to 0.0 or
   1.0, computing b - a and testing it against zero.
 - CMP maps onto CSEL, whose (rA < 0) ? rB : rC * rD is exactly TGSI's CMP.
 - temporaries used to be limited to the eight global registers, and
   overflowed the assert in fp_alu_src_reg(). They now spill into the row
   registers the shader is not using: r0..r3 hold varyings, TEX results and
   the colour output, r4 holds 1/w, so r5..r15 are free.
 - TEX coordinates no longer have to come from a varying. The sampler always
   reads S/T from r0/r1, so a computed coordinate is moved there by an ALU
   packet in a preceding instruction.
 - sampler-only resources keep their natural pitch. A texture descriptor
   carries no stride, so the sampler derives it from the width, and padding
   the pitch to 32 bytes sheared the image.

tests/ holds the harness this was built against: fptest diffs grate against
softpipe, which serves as the oracle, with a tolerance for fp20/fx10
precision. Cases with a varying sample a 3x3 grid, since sampling only the
centre hides interpolation and stride errors. 76/79 pass.

The three failures are the bottom rows of a 5x3 texture, which sample as
zero; NPOT_AUX does not appear to be what the sampler wants there.
