Subject: [PATCH 12/36] grate: implement resource_copy_region, and verify the
 scanout path end to end

resource_copy_region() was a silent no-op, so anything built on a resource
copy quietly kept whatever the destination already held. Route it through
util_resource_copy_region(), which maps both resources - and mapping now
waits for the GPU, so the copy is correct if unhurried.

tests/gbmtest reproduces weston's scanout path exactly: a gbm surface, an EGL
window surface, render, eglSwapBuffers, then lock the front buffer and read it
back through gbm_bo_map. That is the buffer the display scans out, so it
settles what the panel gets without a compositor or a screenshooter in the
way. At 1366x768 it reports every row correct, across several frames and both
buffers of the rotation, and a full frame glReadPixels of the same surface is
correct too.

So the driver is right on the path a compositor actually uses. weston runs on
the panel with the GL renderer, no SMMU faults, no GL errors and no
unimplemented paths hit. Captures taken with weston-screenshooter still show a
band of noise over the bottom quarter, which is not reproducible through any
driver path tested here - gbm_bo_map, full frame glReadPixels and
resource_copy_region are all clean at that size.
