The previous commit took mesa's flip back off for a scanned out buffer, on the
strength of a test that asserted the wrong thing. tests/gbmtest checked the
scanout buffer expecting green to grow downwards, but the shader writes
green = p.y and p.y is 0 at NDC y = -1, which GL puts at the BOTTOM of the
viewport. A scanout buffer is stored top down, so row 0 holds the LARGEST
green. Expecting the opposite is exactly how an upside down display passes.

With the expectation corrected, the unflipped build fails on row 0 - got 0,
wanted 255 - which is the display the panel was showing. Mesa's viewport is
now used as handed over, and the scanout buffer comes out correct on every
row at 800x600, 1024x768 and 1366x768.

gbmtest now checks both conventions in the one run and says which is which:
glReadPixels is bottom up, the buffer behind it is top down.
