From 1fafeb807bc5c0385fd835066a1a73c0b684e841 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Pavlovic <sam@sampavlovic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:13:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/36] grate: make dmabuf import work, which fixes GLX and
 Xwayland

Importing anyone else's buffer failed on its very first syscall. fd_get_size()
opened with lseek(fd, 0, SEEK_CUR) to remember the offset, but the kernel's
dma_buf_llseek() honours only SEEK_END and SEEK_SET and answers EINVAL to
everything else, so the size lookup always failed and grate_bo_import()
returned NULL. Nothing noticed until now because every buffer we had handled
so far was one we allocated ourselves. Seek to the end and rewind to zero.

Two things were missing on the way out as well:

  - resource_get_param() was not implemented at all. DRI3 and the dmabuf
    export path ask for stride, offset and modifier through it, and without
    it they sent DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID to the X server, which answered
    BadAlloc.
  - get_handle() never filled in handle->modifier, leaving whatever the
    caller had there. Every buffer we export is plain linear; say so.

Import and export failures now say which buffer and which syscall failed,
rather than a bare "failed".

Before: glxgears died in dri3_alloc_render_buffer with X error 11, and weston
could not import an Xwayland buffer ("no known conversion for format AR24").
Now glxgears runs on the panel at ~34 fps with no import errors at all.

The tests asked for EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY, which means X11 once mesa is built
with the x11 platform, so they now ask for surfaceless explicitly. Added
tests/primetest.c, which does the export/import round trip on its own.
