From fe0fd2ee8a3770b7840edf9b3afe6d7a3088d9c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Pavlovic <sam@sampavlovic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 21:41:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/36] grate: warn off Xwayland, which hangs the GPU hard
 enough to reboot the device

glamor's shaders need fragment opcodes the compiler does not have and overflow
its 19 scalar temporaries. fp_temp_reg() answers an overflow by returning
register 16 rather than failing the compile, so the malformed program reaches
the GPU, hangs it, and the kernel resets gr3d in a loop until the machine goes
down. Running glxgears under Xwayland reboots a Surface RT.

Wayland clients are unaffected: weston's own shaders compile completely, with
no overflow and no unimplemented opcode, and it runs clean.

Removed --xwayland from the launcher and said so plainly in the packaging
README. The proper fix is to make the register allocator fail the compile
instead of guessing, and then to implement the opcodes.

Also make tests/bg.sh pass the user's supplementary groups through. systemd-run
with --uid/--gid drops them, so weston could not open seatd's socket, which is
group video.
