Subject: [PATCH 21/36] grate: check the program size at runtime, not with an
 assert

b_ndebug is on in the packaged build, so assert(num_fp_instrs < 64) compiled
away and an oversized shader quietly wrote schedule fields that do not fit
their six bits. Complain and clamp instead. A wrong picture is recoverable; a
hung gr3d on a Tegra 3 takes the machine with it.
