From de25b095177118c731f195c35134b361d339aced Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Pavlovic <sam@sampavlovic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:02:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/36] grate: stop enabling a depth unit that does not use the
 depth buffer

The depth unit reads and writes surface 0 - the colour buffer - and ignores the
depth buffer entirely. Clearing the depth buffer to 1.0 or to 0.0 makes no
difference to the test, while the contents of surface 0 decide it.

That is the striping on every lit scene. A colour buffer cleared to opaque
black is BGRA 00 00 00 ff, which read as pairs of 16 bit depths is 0x0000,
0xff00, 0x0000, ... so every second pixel tested against 0.0 and failed and
kept the background. Enabling depth writes additionally had the rasterizer
write depth over the first two bytes per pixel of every colour row, which is
exactly the left half of the framebuffer at 4 bytes per pixel.

Measured and ruled out: QR_Z_TEST's Z_SURF_PTR (every value 0-7 behaves
identically), every other bit of QR_Z_TEST, DW_ST_ENABLE with the depth
surface in and out of the mask, SURFOVERADDR, the OVERLAP descriptor bit,
GLOBAL_FLUSH with each of its cache bits, both Z16 formats, the depth
surface's stride and its BOTTOM_UP flag. Putting the depth buffer in surface 0
instead stops colour reaching the framebuffer at all, so colour has to be
surface 0 and there is nowhere left to point the depth unit.

So it is off unless GRATE_HW_DEPTH is set. The state is still translated, so
turning the switch back on is all it takes to carry on. This costs correct
occlusion, which matters to a 3D app and not to a compositor, and buys a
picture that is flat rather than corrupt: glxgears goes from 47% of adjacent
column pairs differing sharply to 2.9%, which is just the gear edges, and
tests/bigdraw with a depth buffer attached is pixel exact against softpipe
where it was wrong in 28 of 64 columns.

Two real bugs fixed on the way:

  - The gr2d fill writes a 32 bit pattern whatever the pixel size, so a 16 bit
    fill has to be replicated across the word. A depth buffer "cleared" to 1.0
    was coming out as alternating 1.0 and 0.0.
  - grate_compare_func had no case for PIPE_FUNC_GEQUAL, so glDepthFunc
    (GL_GEQUAL) hit UNREACHABLE.

tests/depthtest is a minimal occlusion check against softpipe.
