From 6fb7d356139c18c65bb6b1d7ea08322b42fce441 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Pavlovic <sam@sampavlovic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 14:18:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/36] grate: drop the TGSI translators and compile NIR
 directly

Both stages now translate NIR, so the TGSI paths, the nir_to_tgsi round
trip and the vertex TGSI transform go away, and the screen advertises
NIR as the only IR it takes.

Real shaders needed two things the test suite did not. fcsel had no
translation: the ALU has no select, so it is written as c + mask*(b-c),
with the compare folded into the mask for the fcsel_gt and fcsel_ge
forms. And with one register per value the fragment file ran out on
anything substantial, so a slot now returns to the free list once the
value in it has been read for the last time. Working out where that is
has to look through vecN, fneg and fabs: none of them emit an
instruction, so their sources stay live until whatever consumes the
result, not until the instruction that nominally reads them. Slots are
released only when the instruction being built is emitted, so a pending
operation cannot read a register something else has already reused.
